        "Title": "HOW TO USE:  open the view with the floors.  0 = picture of the tiles (grid, brick, herringbone, straight or 45 deg).  1 = tile size in mm (a picture has no scale): one number = width, the length comes from the picture, or 75 x 190.  2 = AUTO reads the layout from the picture.  It makes a model fill pattern + material and paints the top of the floors (5 = VIEW / SELECTED / NONE).  Move the tiles in Revit: Tab-select a pattern line, Move / Rotate / Align.",
